Hi awesome blavaan folks,

I am playing with the prisamp argument for prior predictive checks. However, I get very long error messages. These look the same and iterative:
Error in chol.default(x, pivot = FALSE) :
  the leading minor of order 10 is not positive definite
Error in pd.solve(varcov, log.det = TRUE) :
  x appears to be not positive definite
Error in chol.default(x, pivot = FALSE) :
  the leading minor of order 10 is not positive definite
Error in pd.solve(varcov, log.det = TRUE) :
  x appears to be not positive definite
Error in chol.default(x, pivot = FALSE) :
  the leading minor of order 11 is not positive definite
Error in pd.solve(varcov, log.det = TRUE) :
  x appears to be not positive definite
Error in chol.default(x, pivot = FALSE) :
  the leading minor of order 11 is not positive definite
Error in pd.solve(varcov, log.det = TRUE) :
  x appears to be not positive definite
Error in chol.default(x, pivot = FALSE) :
  the leading minor of order 11 is not positive definite
Error in pd.solve(varcov, log.det = TRUE) :
  x appears to be not positive definite
Error in chol.default(x, pivot = FALSE) :
  the leading minor of order 10 is not positive definite
Error in pd.solve(varcov, log.det = TRUE) :
  x appears to be not positive definite
Error in chol.default(x, pivot = FALSE) :
  the leading minor of order 9 is not positive definite
Error in pd.solve(varcov, log.det = TRUE) :

Could anyone explain to me why this is happening? Also, I am curious how I can actually approach the prior predictive distribution once the argument works.

I attach the code I used:

library(blavaan)
library(rstan)
options(mc.cores = 2)

model <- '
    # latent variable definitions
    ind60 =~ x1 + x2 + x3
    dem60 =~ y1 + a*y2 + b*y3 + c*y4
    dem65 =~ y5 + a*y6 + b*y7 + c*y8

    # regressions
    dem60 ~ ind60
    dem65 ~ ind60 + dem60

    # residual correlations
    y1 ~~ y5
    y2 ~~ y4 + y6
    y3 ~~ y7
    y4 ~~ y8
    y6 ~~ y8
'

fit <- bsem(model, data=PoliticalDemocracy, n.chains = 2, prisamp = TRUE,
            burnin = 2500, sample = 2500)
summary(fit)

Thanks!

