On Thu, 2020-12-03 at 19:14 -0800, Ihnwhi Heo wrote:
> What I am wondering now is, then, how can I extract both posterior draws and prior predictive draws with the blavInspect() function?
> Or, does the blavInspect(fit, 'mcmc') give prior predictive draws when the prisamp argument is true, whereas the posterior draws are presented when the prisamp argument is false?

Yes, it currently only does one at a time. prisamp=TRUE gives prior samples, while FALSE gives posterior samples.

> I think I am confusing this because, even with the prisamp argument = TRUE, the posterior estimates are still presented with the summary() function.

Are you sure those are posterior estimates in summary()? They should be means and SDs of the prior samples. But the ppp and information criteria are not meaningful... I should probably add a warning about this.

Ed

