That is a good point, I should also change the column labels there. Will add a github issue so I don't forget.

>
> Last additional question, please. I am considering the possibilities of using the prior predictive samples to evaluate the marginal likelihoods with the bridge sampling package. If I set both prisamp argument and mcmcfile argument to TRUE and use the precompiled Stan object from blavaan to fit a model with the stan() function, does the fitted stan fit object still have samples for the prior model? Or, the prisamp() argument is only for the blavaan?

This should still be the prior model. It depends on the data that is being passed in to Stan (the data that is exported with mcmcfile=TRUE). In that data, there are two binary integers: has_data and has_cov. If both equal 0, then you get samples from the prior.

Ed

