| This is a place where the prisamp argument is new, and the blavaan output is not yet labeled informatively. I think that Stan is giving you only the prior log-likelihood, without the data being involved at all. In contrast, blavaan is giving you the likelihood evaluated at the draws from the prior distribution (where the likelihood involves the observed data). I'm not sure what is most useful to you...

