On Tue, 2020-12-08 at 21:02 -0800, Ihnwhi Heo wrote:
> I see. I need to obtain the log marginal likelihood of data drawn from the prior distributions, so I think this is what blavaan does. If possible, how may I debug this within the semstan.rda? Or, do you think I have to investigate this issue via the Stan Discourse?

I think this might be complicated. I think that bridgesampling is relying on the "target" variable in Stan to get the likelihood. But, as soon as the data are involved in the target, Stan will sample from the posterior instead of from the prior. So I'm not sure you can easily do this with the blavaan model.

Ed

