Hi Ihnwhi,

On Mon, 2020-12-14 at 21:03 -0800, Ihnwhi Heo wrote:
> So, yes, I first want Stan to only consider priors and sample draws from them. Next, I hope to use bridgesampling to evaluate those draws from prior distributions. Should it be a very complicated process using the current blavaan and bridgesampling?

I think that the current blavaan model will not work as written. If you start with the blavaan Stan file, I think the best thing to do is move all the priors in the model block to the transformed parameters block, then make "_rng" commands out of them to randomly draw from the priors. This is similar to what happens in simulation-based calibration (see rstan::sbc()). Then run stan() with algorithm="Fixed_param" to evaluate the model likelihood at those priors.

Ed

